<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>61.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <decisions>
        <name>Has_Existing_Handover</name>
        <label>Handover Already Exists?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>242</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Create_Handover</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Handover Yet</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Handover_Exists</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Existing_Handover.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <label>Handover Exists</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Found live 2026-09-20 (full retail cycle test): no automation anywhere in the org ever created an AF_Handover__c record. AF_FL_Handover_SyncOpportunityGate&apos;s own description already assumed &quot;the Quick Action that creates the Handover&quot; existed - it never did; every Handover in this org before today was created by hand or by test-setup Apex. This flow closes that gap: fires the moment an Opportunity reaches Take the Keys (the stage immediately before Closed Won, where the handover checklist actually needs to start), and creates the Handover automatically so a rep is never blocked waiting on a manual step nobody remembered to do. Duplicate-guarded by querying AF_Handover__c.AF_Opportunity__c directly (the real relationship), same pattern as AF_InvoiceSummaryService&apos;s own guard - never trusts the Opportunity&apos;s own AF_Handover__c mirror field, since a partial failure there would otherwise let a second Handover be created on a later re-entry into Take the Keys (e.g. after a stage revert and re-progress).

LFRDN-706 fix: Create_Handover originally only set AF_Opportunity__c and AF_Status__c, leaving AF_Vehicle__c/AF_Contact__c/AF_InvoiceSummary__c blank even though the Opportunity already holds all three by the time it reaches Take the Keys - the rep had to look them up and fill them in by hand, and the Handover record didn&apos;t say which car was being handed to whom until they did. Now copies Opportunity.AF_SelectedVehicle__c / ContactId / AF_InvoiceSummary__c straight onto the new Handover at creation time.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Opp Create Handover On Take The Keys {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Opp Create Handover On Take The Keys</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_Handover</name>
        <label>Create Handover</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>350</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Update_Opportunity_Handover_Link</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_Contact__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.ContactId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_InvoiceSummary__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.AF_InvoiceSummary__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_Opportunity__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_Status__c</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pending</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_Vehicle__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.AF_SelectedVehicle__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>AF_Handover__c</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Existing_Handover</name>
        <label>Get Existing Handover</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Has_Existing_Handover</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>AF_Opportunity__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>AF_Handover__c</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Update_Opportunity_Handover_Link</name>
        <label>Set Opportunity Handover Link</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>458</locationY>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_Handover__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Create_Handover</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>Opportunity</object>
    </recordUpdates>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Existing_Handover</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterFormula>ISPICKVAL({!$Record.StageName}, &quot;Take the Keys&quot;) &amp;&amp; ISCHANGED({!$Record.StageName})</filterFormula>
        <object>Opportunity</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Update</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
